Ask the Harbourmaster about that.	這件事去問港務司吧。
They are ports held by Muslim rulers.	那些是由穆斯林統治者掌控的港口。
Brittany, or Bretagne, is held by wild and unruly Celtic tribes known as Gauls.	布列塔尼，法語稱作 Bretagne，是桀驁不馴的凱爾特部族「高盧人」的領地。
Dublin is on the island of Eire.	都柏林位於愛爾蘭島上。
Rennes is in the land of the Franks, across the channel.	勒恩位於海峽對岸的法蘭克人之地。
Rome was once the center of the Roman Empire, but the power of this ancient city has much declined.	羅馬曾是羅馬帝國的中心，但這座古城如今國勢已大不如前。
Thessalonica is in northern Greece, above Athens.	帖撒羅尼迦位於希臘北部，在雅典以北。
Gaza is at the easternmost end of the Mediterranean Sea.	加薩位於地中海最東端。
An Irish legend says Conal Cearnach was a prisoner of the Romans in Jerusalem and witnessed the crucifixion of Christ.	愛爾蘭傳說道，科納爾·柯納赫曾在耶路撒冷淪為羅馬人的階下囚，親眼目睹了基督被釘上十字架。
Frastrada was a wife of Charlemagne, ruler of the Franks.  Rumour said she was a witch from the East.	芙拉斯特拉妲是法蘭克人統治者查理曼的妻子之一。傳聞她是來自東方的女巫。
The legendary founders of Rome were twin brothers, Remus and Romulus, who were suckled by a she-wolf.	羅馬傳說中的建城者，是由母狼哺育長大的雙生兄弟——羅慕路斯與雷穆斯。
The powerful Greek Goddess, Athene, is the patroness of sailors.  The city of Athens is named after her.	強大的希臘女神雅典娜，是水手的守護神。雅典城便是以她之名命名。
The name Al-Uzza, means "Powerful One".  It was the title of an Arabic Goddess associated with the founding of Mohammed's tribe.	Al-Uzza 之名意為「強大者」，是與穆罕默德所屬部族建立淵源的一位阿拉伯女神的稱號。
That is a matter to discuss with the Harbourmaster.	這件事該找港務司商議。
This is a foreign merchant's ship, not subject to your whim, King Arthur.	這是一艘外國商船，不受你隨心差遣，亞瑟王。
That is work for sailors, not a warrior-king.	那是水手的活計，不是戰士之王該做的事。
He is doing his duty and will move only when he should move.  As a king, you must set an example and respect him as master of this port.	他正在履行職責，該動身時自會動身。身為君王，你必須以身作則，尊重他作為此港之主的身分。
Not a wise idea, Arthur.	這不是個明智的主意，亞瑟。
Arthur! Do not disgrace yourself by threatening this good man.	亞瑟！休要威脅這位善良之人，那有失你的體面。
I do not mean to anger you, m'lud, but it is my duty to collect fare before a passenger may board a ship.	老爺，我無意觸怒您，但收取船資本是我的職責所在，乘客得先付清才能登船。
The purse itself is of no value to him.  And you may yet need it.	這錢囊本身對他並無用處，而你或許還用得上。
You already did that during your ride here.  No need to do it again now.	你騎馬前來時已經做過此事，此刻無須再做一次。
That would be absurd.	那未免太荒謬了。
The sharp tang of salt water mingles with the pungent smell of fish.	海水的鹹澀氣息與魚腥的刺鼻味道交織在一起。
The wooden ship creaks and bumps against the pier.  Water washes across wood and stone and waves dash upon the shore.  Seagulls cry raucously from above.	木船嘎吱作響，一次次撞上碼頭。潮水沖刷過木板與石塊，浪花拍打著岸邊。海鷗在頭頂上刺耳地鳴叫著。
You must be on a horse to get off a horse.	你得先騎在馬上，才能從馬上下來。
Enter destination:	輸入目的地：
Weary days and nights march on. A storm catches the ship and you are forced to lend your strong back to the efforts of the crew to save themselves.	疲憊的晝夜一天天過去。一場暴風雨襲上船身，你被迫拿出強健的臂膀，協助船員們奮力自救。
Huge waves crash across the decks. You barely save your mule, but your pack and nearly all your belongings are washed away.	巨浪不斷打上甲板。你好不容易保住了騾子，行囊與幾乎所有的隨身物品卻都被沖走了。
The next day, the Captain thanks you by giving good advice, "You are not a king in these lands, so do not be quick to draw your sword for you will be surrounded by enemies. Be careful who you trust and never pay bribes with too much coin."	翌日，船長以一番忠告向你道謝：「在這片土地上，你並非君王，切莫輕易拔劍，否則將四面楚歌。慎選信任之人，行賄時也別出手太闊綽。」
You join the crew in sharing several rounds of wine as they wait for the tide to change so they may enter Gaza port.	船員們等候潮水轉向以便駛入加薩港時，你也加入他們，一同暢飲了幾巡酒。
The wine flows freely after such a long and arduous journey. Soon, you fall into a very deep, dreamless sleep.	歷經這段漫長艱辛的旅程，美酒暢流不絕。不久，你便沉入一場無夢的深眠。
The skilled Captain beats past Celtic Brittany with all speed thanks to good winds.	憑藉著順風之助，經驗老到的船長全速繞過了凱爾特人的布列塔尼。
At Malaga you get your first sight of those who worship Islam.  Their manners and dress are strange to you, yet they are hospitable to any man who worships the one god, no matter by what name he is called.	在馬拉加，你頭一回見到信奉伊斯蘭教的人。他們的舉止與衣著在你眼中十分陌生，但無論那唯一真神被稱作什麼名字，他們對敬奉祂的人都同樣好客。
In Tunis the worshippers of Allah seem much the same but are ruled instead by the Aghlabid Emirate under the Abbasid Empire.	在突尼斯，敬奉阿拉的人看來大同小異，只是此地統治者換成了臣屬於阿拔斯帝國的阿格拉布王朝。
As you approach Athens, a corsair filled with Saracen pirates overtakes your ship.	船隻將近雅典時，一艘滿載撒拉遜海盜的海盜船追上了你們。
You fight like the great warrior you are, but the Saracens are many and merciless. You are finally cut down and thrown to the fish.	你如身經百戰的偉大戰士般奮力搏殺，但撒拉遜人人多勢眾又冷酷無情。你終究寡不敵眾，倒下後被拋屍餵魚。
A quick voyage brings you to the northern coast of Brittany where you are tragically dashed to death upon jagged rocks.	一段短暫的航程將你帶到布列塔尼北岸，你卻在那裡不幸撞上嶙峋礁岩，慘遭滅頂。
Many days and nights pass in cramped discomfort.  The coastline of Muslim-held Iberia glides past.	許多晝夜在侷促難耐中流逝。穆斯林治下的伊比利亞海岸線緩緩掠過眼前。
You land briefly in Tunis, ruled by the Muslims of the Aghlabid Emirate under the Abbasid Empire.  Soon you will reach Rome.	你在突尼斯短暫靠岸，此地由臣屬阿拔斯帝國的阿格拉布王朝穆斯林統治。不久你便將抵達羅馬。
Approaching Rome, your ship is caught in a powerful storm. You are washed overboard and your armour quickly drags you to the bottom of the sea.	船隻將近羅馬時，遭遇一場猛烈的暴風雨。你被捲落海中，一身盔甲迅速將你拖向海底。
Captain beats his way expertly up St. George's Channel toward Dublin.	船長熟練地引領船隻，逆流而上駛過聖喬治海峽，朝都柏林前進。
Alas, a longship of crazed Vikings falls upon the ship.  Excaliber sings from its sheath and does mighty work.  The decks run red, but you are overwhelmed and killed in combat with a berserker.	唉，一艘滿載瘋狂維京人的長船撲上船來。聖劍出鞘鏗鏘作響，大顯神威。甲板血染一片，但你終究寡不敵眾，命喪一名狂戰士之手。
Oh, no, this mukhtar is an evil man and would make you a slave.  He must not find you.	噢，不好，這位村長是個惡人，會把你賣去為奴。絕不能讓他發現你。
Oh, sir, I could not keep her.  And you will need her for your journey.	噢，大人，我不能留下牠。您這趟旅程還用得著牠呢。
I am not allowed to accept gifts, sir, except from my Master.	大人，我不得收受餽贈，除非是我主人給的。
I am not allowed to accept gifts for doing my duty, sir.	大人，我不得因盡本分而收受餽贈。
You cannot seek it in Gaza, sir, or the mukhtar will imprison you.  Perhaps my Master can help you with this problem.	大人，您不能在加薩尋訪此事，否則村長會將您下獄。或許我主人能助您解決這個難題。
I have never been anywhere but Gaza, but my Master can surely answer you.	我除了加薩之外哪裡都沒去過，但我主人必定能回答您。
It is true my Master is poor, but he is a good man and he knows so many things.  And while you speak with Al-Sirat, I can care for your poor mule after her long sea journey.	我主人確實貧窮，但他是個好人，懂得的事情極多。您與 Al-Sirat 交談之時，我可以照料您那頭長途航行後疲憊的騾子。
Please do not delay long, sir.  Gaza is no longer safe for foreigners and no man here will aid you in any way except my Master.	大人，請莫要耽擱太久。加薩對外地人來說已不再安全，此地除了我主人之外，沒有人會出手相助。
Sa'alam aleikem	Sa'alam aleikem
Sa'alam aleikem.  Peace be unto you.	Sa'alam aleikem，祝你平安。
He is a young boy, poor but healthy, with an open, honest face and intelligence in his eyes.	他是個年幼的男孩，雖然窮困卻很健康，面容坦率誠懇，眼神透著聰慧。
Please come and ask my Master.  He knows so much more than I.	請隨我去問問我主人，他懂得的遠比我多。
Al-Sirat will know.  He is the most learned of men.	Al-Sirat 必定知曉，他是天底下最有學問的人。
He did not choose to visit my Master, but hurried off into the desert alone.	他沒有選擇去拜訪我主人，而是獨自匆匆奔進了沙漠。
Sir, my Master is the wisest man in the whole world.  He can answer any question.  Please, let us go to him.	大人，我主人是全世界最有智慧的人，任何問題他都答得出來。請隨我去見他吧。
Ignore the brat and let us do business.  The mukhtar could have spies about, so we should act quickly.  You have no pack, I see, and no waterskin.  You can buy nothing in Gaza without being arrested.	別理那小鬼，咱們談正事吧。村長恐怕布有眼線，我們得盡快行動。我瞧您沒有行囊，也沒有水袋。在加薩，您買什麼都會被逮捕。
Therefore, you must surely hire me to take you through the desert and lead you from one waterhole to the next. That is the only way you will reach Jerusalem alive.	因此，您勢必得雇我帶您穿越沙漠，領您從一處水坑走到下一處水坑。唯有如此，您才能活著抵達耶路撒冷。
You want to avoid the mukhtar.  I give you good advice.  Trust me in all things.	您想避開村長，我這是給您的良言。凡事都信我便是。
No man in Gaza will deal with you because of the mukhtar's edicts.  If you are spotted by his men, you will be arrested.	因為村長的禁令，加薩沒有人敢與您打交道。若被他的人瞧見，您便會被逮捕。
Most generous, habib.  She will make a fine payment for being your guide, if you let me take you to Jerusalem.	真慷慨啊，朋友。若您讓我帶您前往耶路撒冷，牠便是上好的嚮導酬勞。
An odd looking trinket, but of no interest to me.	這件小玩意兒模樣古怪，但我沒興趣。
I am content to wait until I bring you safely to Jerusalem to receive my reward.	我甘願等到平安帶您抵達耶路撒冷後，再收取酬勞。
Trust me in all things.  Only I know the secret paths of the desert and where to find water.  Only I can guide you safely through.	凡事都信我便是。唯有我知曉沙漠中的密徑與水源何在，也唯有我能領您安然穿越。
He looks a dry and hard man, as one might look from a lifetime in harsh deserts.	他看起來乾瘦而剛硬，正是在嚴酷沙漠中度過一生之人的模樣。
Ignore the brat and let us do business.	別理那小鬼，咱們談正事吧。
He is an impoverished old scholar.  Do not waste your time with him.	他不過是個窮困潦倒的老學究，別在他身上浪費時間。
Never heard of it.	從未聽聞。
Trust me in all things.  I can lead you safely to all waterholes and wadis.	凡事都信我便是。我能領您安然抵達每一處水坑與乾河谷。
There was another like you, but he was gone from here before I could offer my services.	之前也有個像您這樣的人來過，但我還沒來得及自薦，他就已經離開此地了。
If you must ask questions, let us at least get started on the trip and talk later.	您若非問不可，咱們至少先上路，有話待會兒再說。
It is an old tower on a spit of land.	那是一座建在沙嘴上的古塔。
The sail was carefully repaired after the storm.	風暴過後，船帆已細心修補過了。
By my beard, you must know every plank of the ship by now, having been aboard for weeks.	憑我這把鬍子起誓，您在船上待了數週，想必連每一塊船板都認熟了。
Though the mule is here, she looks even more unhappy than when you started this trip.	騾子雖然在這兒，但牠看起來比啟程時還要更不高興。
The rocks alongside the dock are slippery.  Avoid them.	碼頭邊的岩石很滑，須避開。
This is one of the stone docks at Gaza port.	這是加薩港的一座石造碼頭。
I would strongly advise you to heed this boy.	我強烈建議您聽從這孩子的話。
I would advise you to remember the advice the Captain offered you during the voyage.	我建議您記住船長在航程中給您的忠告。
It is not clear what you want.  Try to be more specific.	看不出你想要什麼，說得再明確些。
I suspect that no matter how hard you look, you will not find Al-Sirat or Hazm again.	我猜想，無論你如何搜尋，都不會再找到 Al-Sirat 或哈慈了。
You should have paid more attention to Hazm.  You would undoubtedly know a great deal more than you do now.	你當初該多留意哈慈的話。如此一來，你此刻懂得的必定遠比現在多。
There is no guide here.  You are on your own.	這裡沒有嚮導，你只能靠自己了。
From what we have heard, the mukhtar is the last man you wish to find.  Or to have find you.  You should dally here no longer.	據我們所聞，村長正是你最不想遇見的人——也最不想被他找到。你不該再在此逗留。
You will have to make do with what you have or can find.	你只能將就手邊擁有或能找到的東西了。
You should be well and truly sick of this ship by now.	此刻你想必早已對這艘船厭煩透頂了。
It seems I must warn you often that such violent urges against those who have done you no wrong will stain your soul and make you unworthy of the Grail.	看來我得常常提醒你：對無辜之人動用如此暴戾的衝動，將玷污你的靈魂，使你不配獲得聖杯。
Unfortunately, you lost nearly everything when the storm washed your pack overboard.	很不幸，那場暴風雨把你的行囊沖落海中，你幾乎失去了一切。
All seaports share similar odors, mainly the tang of salt and fish.	所有海港氣味都大同小異，主要是海鹽與魚腥的味道。
It has been emptied.  Do not waste your time.	裡頭已經空了，別浪費時間。
Thank you, sir, but I cannot accept money.  My reward is serving my Master well.	謝謝您，大人，但我不能收下錢財。好好侍奉我主人，便是我的酬報。
You have no business doing so.	你沒有理由這麼做。
It would appear that you slept through the entire unloading of the ship.  Even the crew is gone.	看來你把整段卸貨的過程都睡過去了，如今連船員都已離去。
Before you lies the sun-baked village of Gaza.  Beyond the town lie hills, and beyond them is the desert.	眼前是烈日曝曬下的加薩村落，村落之外是丘陵，丘陵之外便是沙漠。
The land rises in rocky hills to the east.	東邊的地勢隆起，盡是嶙峋的丘陵。
Only Hazm could have shown you the way.  You should have followed him when you had the chance.	唯有哈慈能為你指路。有機會時，你就該跟著他走。
I presume he is with his Master.	我猜他是跟主人在一起。
It is now quite empty.	如今已空無一物。
It has been removed.	已被移走。
It is made of stone, part of an old fortification.	這是石造的，屬於一座古老防禦工事的一部分。
It is built of stone, solid and functional.	以石塊建成，堅固而實用。
You have been looking at the waves for week upon weary week.  There is nothing new to see.	你已經望著這片波浪看了一個又一個疲憊的星期，沒什麼新鮮事可看了。
At this moment, everything you possess is upon your person, except for your mule.	此刻，除了那頭騾子，你所擁有的一切都在你身上。
Aye, 'tis a mast.  It holds the sail.	正是，那是桅杆，用來撐起船帆。
Aye, it connects the ship to the dock.	正是，它將船與碼頭相連。
It looks the same as it has for weeks.	看起來和這幾週以來一模一樣。
They are gone.	他們已經離去。
He is gone.	他已經離去。
It has a rudder, as might be expected.	不出所料，它裝有一具船舵。
There is a tower on a spit of land and other hills in the distance in one direction, and the town of Gaza in the other.	一邊是沙嘴上的塔樓與遠方隱約的丘陵，另一邊則是加薩鎮。
It is not much to look at it.  Poor dwellings, empty streets, much dirt and an air of hostility.	這裡沒什麼好看的。破舊的屋舍、空盪的街道、遍地塵土，還瀰漫著一股敵意。
Aye, they are pleasant enough, as clouds go.	是啊，就雲朵而言，它們看起來還算宜人。
It is a valley cut into the earth by running water. Sometimes a wadi will still have water, but often they are dry.	那是一道被流水切鑿而成的谷地。乾河谷有時仍存有水，但多半是乾涸的。
I have much book knowledge, but I cannot guide you step by step to a place where I have never been.	我雖飽讀詩書，卻無法一步步引領你前往一個我從未去過的地方。
You are the wisest of men, sir, except for my Master!  Please follow me.	大人，您是天下最有智慧的人——僅次於我主人！請隨我來。
The desert lies ahead.  You will never cross it without my help.	沙漠就在前方。沒有我的幫助，你絕不可能穿越它。
You need not pay now, but I could not insult your generosity by refusing.  Let us set out at once!	您現在無須付錢，但拒絕您的慷慨對我而言未免失禮。咱們這就啟程吧！
Excellent!  Let us waste no time! Follow me.	太好了！咱們別浪費時間了，跟我來。
Oh, sir!  I am so happy you have returned!	噢，大人！您回來了，我真是太高興了！
Please, will you come with me now and accept the hospitality of my Master, Al-Sirat?	請問，您現在願意隨我同去，接受我主人 Al-Sirat 的款待嗎？
Al-Sirat is only poor in worldly goods, but in knowledge and wisdom he is the richest man on earth!	Al-Sirat 雖然家財微薄，但論知識與智慧，他卻是天底下最富有的人！
If you change your mind, sir, I will still gladly lead you to him.  But I must return to him soon, either with or without you.	大人，您若改變心意，我仍樂意領您去見他。但無論您是否同行，我都得儘快回到他身邊。
You are the wisest of men, sir, except for my Master!   Please follow me.	大人，您是天下最有智慧的人——僅次於我主人！請隨我來。
Your armour and steel drag you to the bottom and there you will lie until you are rotten, soggy and pulpy and truly forgotten.	你的盔甲與鋼鐵把你拖向海底，你將長眠於此，直到腐朽、泡爛、化為一團爛泥，徹底被世人遺忘。
You should not think of returning to Gaza, Arthur.  If the mukhtar's men find you, it will mean your life.	亞瑟，你不該考慮回加薩去。若被村長的人發現，你將性命不保。
A pity.  You are so young to die.  Well, we may yet meet again, in case you change your mind.	可惜了，你這般年輕便要喪命。罷了，若你改變心意，咱們或許還能再見。
He does not answer.	他沒有回應。
He could never hear you from here.	他在這裡絕不可能聽見你的聲音。
